Wildcards
description: any string key, any position - and what a plain index never sees
- >
  `?` as a portion matches **every string-keyed entry** of the current node; `[?]` matches **every
  position** - all entries, keyed or not, *including* entries created by anchors. `?` is the keyed
  subset, and a query may open with a wildcard.
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  team: ?              → :team:alice, :team:bob
  pets: ?              → ∅            (pets has only keyless entries)
  pets[?]              → :pets:0, :pets:1
  pets[?]: name        → :pets:0:name, :pets:1:name
  : tags: whole[?]     → :thirty      (an &...[] membership)
- >
  A bare position stays a pointer step: it addresses the container's own entry n and **never** an
  anchor-created member - no position claims - so `: tags: whole: 0` is empty.
